From: dresden196 <50474030+dresden196@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] NickelOS: Linux apps ask for the camera

Flatpak apps reach the webcams only through xdg-desktop-portal's Camera
portal (PipeWire nodes; nickel-session's WirePlumber monitors V4L2), which
it offers only with an Access backend. xdg-desktop-portal-nickel's Access
asks Chrome:

- VmApplicationsService.NickelAccessAsk(app id, app name, title, body,
  grant label, deny label, icon) answers "allow", "deny" or "off".
  NickelAccess asks in ChromeOS's system dialog ("Allow Sober to use the
  camera?", Allow / Don't allow); the portal remembers the answer per app.
  When camera access is off in Privacy controls it says so and offers the
  settings instead ("off", which the portal does not remember). Requests
  other than the camera show the portal's own words. Esc answers no (Ash's
  system dialog has no key for its cancel button).

Found with Sober (Roblox): its sign-in challenge runs in WebKitGTK, which
asks for the camera; with no Camera portal the request failed without a
prompt and the challenge never finished.

